PARRYING
========

  attacker                       defender
  --------                       --------
  swing        --->  roll  --->  parry?  ---> yes ---> no damage
                                   |
                                   no
                                   |
                                   v
                                 armour ---> damage

A parry is a defence channel: you have one if you hold the trait, and you do
not if you do not. Nothing needs configuring for that to be true — presence is
decided by storage, which is the same rule every trait in this game follows.

Holding no defence channel at all is not a bug and not a penalty. You get one
implicit dodge worth the whole pool, which is what a creature that nobody has
thought about yet should do.

This file has no extension, so the help system shows it exactly as it is
written — no headings, no bullets, no reflowing. That is what you want for a
diagram; the moment a paragraph gets rewrapped the arrows above stop pointing
at anything.
